 "title": "cosh x = 2",
 "caption": "The curve y = cosh x = (eˣ + e⁻ˣ)/2 has its minimum 1 at x = 0 and is symmetric. It meets y = 2 at x = ±ln(2 + √3) ≈ ±1.317, where eˣ = 2 ± √3.",
 "alt": "The graph of y = cosh x, a symmetric U-shape with minimum (0, 1), and the line y = 2 meeting it at x ≈ −1.317 and x ≈ 1.317.",
 "description": [
  "cosh x = (eˣ + e⁻ˣ)/2 is symmetric about the y-axis with minimum 1.",
  "cosh x = 2 gives u² − 4u + 1 = 0 with u = eˣ, so u = 2 ± √3.",
  "Then x = ln(2 + √3) ≈ 1.317 or x = ln(2 − √3) = −1.317."
